onnect, timeout, output limit, exception, shutdown and worker crash/restart. Empty-cgroup and file-removal proof required; cleanup failure makes worker unhealthy and blocks admission.\nAC6: Exclusive-lock journaled Nuke/pkexec deployment stages and verifies worker before MCP, preserves unrelated config/data, backs up/restores both binary trees/manifests/units/drop-ins/policy/YAML and active/enabled/masked plus linger states. Inject failures/restarts at every transition; incomplete journal recovered before update. RecoveryFailed retains backups and stopped admission; rollback never claims helper goal fixed.\nAC7: TDD red evidence before code; full current/prior applicable unit suites and required integration/deployment scopes have zero failures and zero skips. Independent phase reviews with durable full request/response JSONL and logged verdict/readback, final accuracy/completeness >=98 before any done state. Explicit operator architecture approval required before implementation; no approval or implementation is claimed by this capture.",
