      "body": "### FR-QB-004 (New): Enforced completion obligations\nTR-QB-COMPLETION-001 (New): Await a pre-completion gate for completion tools, text-only replies, success events, and final delivery; verification matches current changed state.\n- AC-QB-010: Successful final-answer payloads/success events remain withheld until required checks pass; blocked or incomplete diagnostics remain deliverable without claiming success. TEST-QB-010: gates_all_successful_completion_paths. TDD: P1.\n- AC-QB-011: Code/doc edits and command-made changes invalidate stale evidence; failed/missing applicable checks block completion. TEST-QB-011: blocks_completion_on_failed_missing_or_stale_verification. TDD: P1.\n- AC-QB-012: A host-owned classifier derives phaseId and phaseClosing from trusted governed TODO/task mutations and MCP records, never model prose. It classifies operationClass from that trusted state plus source fingerprints: any working-tree content change within the verification-policy scope is development, whether made by an edit tool or command; administrative turns have unchanged source contents and only TODO, requirement or session-record effects. Administrative turns carry no verification or HV obligation; development turns complete only after required verification passes for the current fingerprint; a mutation completing a task or setting done: true on a TODO listed as phase-gated by the signed workspace verification policy is rejected without a valid HV receipt; for this workspace the policy lists QB-AGENT-001 tasks prefixed P1: through P5: and Final:, and done: true on QB-AGENT-001; TODOs without a phase-gate entry carry no HV obligation. TEST-QB-012: classifies_operations_and_gates_phase_closure_on_verified_hv_receipt (administrative, development, valid receipt, forged receipt, stale receipt). TDD: P1. Valid receipt: read back through the supported plugin from a completed MCP turn whose session agent identity is the configured reviewer identity (ClaudeCode), not